    "Same structure as content/routines/strong-foundations-6-weeks.json. Exercise details live in content/exercises/strength-catalogue.json.",
    "Each phase defines its day templates; every week in that phase repeats them.",
    "Lighter week: use about 60 to 70% of the normal sets (round down, minimum 1) at the same weights, with 3 reps in reserve.",
    "Exercises sharing a superset_group are done back to back, resting after the pair.",
    "Draft for coach review before launch.",
    "Complete week (AGENTS.md W1, W5, W6, W7): weekly_schedule has one 7-day template per profiles.cardio_preference (avoid, fine, love). Routines with cardio_balanced=true use the same template for everyone.",
    "Complete week: strength slots point at the phase day (day_key). Cardio and recovery slots point at support_days, which pick the cardio session or stretch routine by week.",
    "Complete week: a finisher is a cardio block after the strength block on that day (block order warmup, strength, cardio_finisher, cooldown). It's skipped in finisher_skip_weeks (checkpoint and lighter weeks), and she can skip it with one tap at any time.",
    "Complete week: weekdays are defaults. If she picked different training days, place strength days on her days in order, then fill cardio on free days (avoid the day before a lower-body or full-body day where possible), recovery on a free day after a lower-body or full-body day, and keep at least one full rest day.",
    "Complete week: optional slots are suggestions. They count towards the week when done but aren't part of the weekly target Y. Y = planned_sessions in weekly_structure_summary.",
    "Complete week: lighter week cardio uses the session at its starting length with an easy-effort note. Cardio counts towards the weekly target and streak, never towards strength personal bests."
